---
import { COST_BUYING_MODELS } from '@/lib/seo/barbershopWebsiteCostPage';
---

<section class="bwcost-section bwcost-models" id="cost-options" aria-labelledby="bwcost-models-heading">
  <div class="bwcost-section__inner">
    <header class="bwcost-section__header">
      <h2 id="bwcost-models-heading" class="bwcost-section__title">What are you actually paying for?</h2>
      <p class="bwcost-section__lede">
        A one-page website and a booking-led shop platform solve different problems. Start with what your shop
        needs, then compare the full price.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="bwcost-table-wrap">
      <table class="bwcost-table">
        <caption class="bwcost-sr-only">
          Four buying models for a barbershop website and what each is best suited to
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Buying model</th>
            <th scope="col">Best suited to</th>
            <th scope="col">Main question / limitation</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            COST_BUYING_MODELS.map((row) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{row.model}</th>
                <td data-label="Best suited to">{row.bestSuitedTo}</td>
                <td data-label="Main question / limitation">{row.mainQuestion}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="bwcost-models__decision">
      If you only need a simple brochure site, a separate website purchase may be cheaper. If you need customers
      to choose services, barbers and time slots and want to manage the bookings too, compare the integrated
      option.
    </p>

    <aside class="bwcost-inset" aria-labelledby="bwcost-four-chair">
      <h3 id="bwcost-four-chair" class="bwcost-inset__title">What should a four-chair barbershop check?</h3>
      <p>
        Imagine a barbershop with four active chairs. A basic site can show the team, prices and location. But if
        customers need to choose a particular barber and an available appointment time, ask whether the quoted
        price includes individual availability, online booking, confirmations and a usable shop diary — or whether
        a separate subscription is required.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <div class="bwcost-anatomy" aria-labelledby="bwcost-anatomy-heading">
      <h3 id="bwcost-anatomy-heading" class="bwcost-anatomy__title">What's included — and what could cost extra?</h3>
      <ol class="bwcost-anatomy__list">
        <li>
          <strong>Building the site</strong>
          <span>Design or initial setup, pages, brand assets, content and revisions — one-off or included.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Running the site</strong>
          <span>Domain registration and renewals; hosting, SSL, updates, support and changes.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Taking bookings and payments</strong>
          <span>
            Booking-button redirect versus integrated service/barber/time selection; standalone booking fees and
            card-processing costs.
          </span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Control when leaving</strong>
          <span>Domain and content rights, source code/templates, data export, term and post-cancellation hosting.</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="bwcost-anatomy__takeaway">
        Ask for an itemised price covering the build, domain, hosting, booking software, payments, support and the
        terms if you leave.
      </p>
      <p class="bwcost-anatomy__link">
        <a href="/barbershop-online-booking">See how online booking works</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
